  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO: Tbilisi School of Political Studies (TSPS) &#x2013; September Seminar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tbilisi School of Political Studies (TSPS) is a leading NGO dedicated to training young professionals and civil servants in democratic governance. In Georgia, this entails fostering dialogue on key issues such as democratic transformation, free and fair elections, institutional strengthening, decentralisation, civic engagement, and the development of a resilient civil society.  The TSPS autumn seminar will bring together experts drawn from the fields of academia, civil society, journalists and the diplomatic community, to discuss challenges and identify potential solutions relating to democratic backsliding and Georgia&#x2019;s turning away from the Euro-Atlantic pathway.
  
UK support for this event will allow us to support work to bring together thought leaders working in diverse fields, to discuss the challenges currently facing Georgia and identify a way forward.  It will allow the British Embassy Tbilisi to deepen our engagement with experts working in the fields of democracy and governance, influence partners&#x2019; approaches, and demonstrate UK thought leadership.  As a result of the conference, we will identify practical steps we take take in coordination with partners to protect democratic space and counter authoritarian trends in Georgia.</narrative>
  </description>
